n=b8?"Cut moves and pauses in F2L \u2013 half of your solve time.":"Gi\u1ea3m s\u1ed1 b\u01b0\u1edbc v\xe0 s\u1ed1 l\u1ea7n d\u1eebng \u1edf F2L \u2013 ph\u1ea7n chi\u1ebfm n\u1eeda th\u1eddi gian gi\u1ea3i."
m=b8?"No fixed order: each time pick the EASIEST pair (visible in the top layer, fewest moves).":"Kh\xf4ng l\xe0m theo th\u1ee9 t\u1ef1 c\u1ed1 \u0111\u1ecbnh: m\u1ed7i l\u1ea7n ch\u1ecdn c\u1eb7p D\u1ec4 nh\u1ea5t (\u0111\xe3 l\u1ed9 ra \u1edf t\u1ea7ng tr\xean, \xedt b\u01b0\u1edbc nh\u1ea5t)."
l=b8?"Insert into back slots with R' U' R or L U L' instead of rotating y2 (see lesson F2L 4).":"Ch\xe8n v\xe0o khe sau b\u1eb1ng R' U' R ho\u1eb7c L U L' thay v\xec xoay y2 (xem b\xe0i F2L 4)."
k=b8?"Pair at the back of the top layer: turn U to bring it forward \u2013 a U turn beats a cube rotation.":"C\u1eb7p \u1edf m\u1eb7t sau t\u1ea7ng tr\xean: xoay U \u0111\u01b0a ra tr\u01b0\u1edbc r\u1ed3i m\u1edbi x\u1eed l\xfd \u2013 U nhanh h\u01a1n xoay c\u1ea3 cube."
j=b8?"Use an empty slot to set up a pair: an unsolved slot can be used to split/join instead of a long sequence.":"D\xf9ng khe tr\u1ed1ng \u0111\u1ec3 gh\xe9p c\u1eb7p: n\u1ebfu m\u1ed9t khe ch\u01b0a l\xe0m, c\xf3 th\u1ec3 d\xf9ng n\xf3 \u0111\u1ec3 t\xe1ch/gh\xe9p thay cho b\u01b0\u1edbc r\u01b0\u1eddm r\xe0."
m=A.a([m,l,k,j,b8?"While inserting a pair, your eyes should already be finding the next one (see Trick 10: Look-ahead).":"Ch\xe8n xong c\u1eb7p n\xe0y, m\u1eaft \u0111\xe3 ph\u1ea3i t\xecm c\u1eb7p ti\u1ebfp theo (xem Trick 10: Nh\xecn tr\u01b0\u1edbc)."],s)
b8=$.c==="en"
l=b8?"Back-right \xb7 ready pair":"Sau-ph\u1ea3i \xb7 c\u1eb7p s\u1eb5n"
b8=b8?"Back-left \xb7 ready pair":"Sau-tr\xe1i \xb7 c\u1eb7p s\u1eb5n"
k=t.sM
b8=A.a([new A.b_("f2l_br_in",l,"R' U' R",""),new A.b_("f2l_bl_in",b8,"L U L'","")],k)
l=$.c==="en"
j=l?"F2L tricks: stuck pairs, empty slots, white facing up":"M\u1eb9o F2L: c\u1eb7p k\u1eb9t, khe tr\u1ed1ng, g\xf3c tr\u1eafng h\u01b0\u1edbng l\xean"
i=l?"Handle the F2L situations that make you pause the longest.":"X\u1eed l\xfd g\u1ecdn nh\u1eefng th\u1ebf F2L hay l\xe0m b\u1ea1n d\u1eebng l\u1ea1i l\xe2u nh\u1ea5t."
h=l?"Pair stuck in another slot: take it out with that slot's own insert (front-left: L' U L) \u2013 ideally inserting the front-left pair at the same time if it's waiting on top. Then adjust U and insert the freed pair where it belongs.":"C\u1eb7p b\u1ecb k\u1eb9t trong khe kh\xe1c: l\u1ea5y ra b\u1eb1ng ch\xednh c\xf4ng th\u1ee9c ch\xe8n c\u1ee7a khe \u0111\xf3 (khe tr\u01b0\u1edbc-tr\xe1i: L' U L), \u0111\u1ed3ng th\u1eddi \u0111\u01b0a \u0111\u01b0\u1ee3c c\u1eb7p c\u1ee7a khe tr\u01b0\u1edbc-tr\xe1i v\xe0o lu\xf4n n\u1ebfu n\xf3 \u0111ang ch\u1edd \u1edf tr\xean. Sau \u0111\xf3 ch\u1ec9nh U v\xe0 ch\xe8n c\u1eb7p v\u1eeba l\u1ea5y ra v\xe0o \u0111\xfang khe."
g=l?"An empty slot is a workspace: when the corner and edge are awkward on top, push one piece into an unsolved slot, turn U to line up the other, then pull it back out as a pair \u2013 instead of a long split sequence.":"Khe tr\u1ed1ng l\xe0 ch\u1ed7 \u0111\u1ec3 gh\xe9p t\u1ea1m: khi g\xf3c v\xe0 c\u1ea1nh kh\xf3 gh\xe9p \u1edf t\u1ea7ng tr\xean, c\xf3 th\u1ec3 \u0111\u1ea9y m\u1ed9t kh\u1ed1i xu\u1ed1ng khe ch\u01b0a l\xe0m, xoay U cho kh\u1ed1i kia t\u1edbi \u0111\xfang ch\u1ed7 r\u1ed3i k\xe9o l\xean th\xe0nh c\u1eb7p \u2013 thay cho chu\u1ed7i d\xe0i \u0111\u1ec3 t\xe1ch c\u1eb7p."
f=l?"White facing up: don't pair it straight away. Put the corner right above the slot, use R U2 R' (or F' U2 F) to turn it into a white-sideways case, then insert normally.":"G\xf3c tr\u1eafng h\u01b0\u1edbng l\xean: \u0111\u1eebng gh\xe9p ngay. \u0110\u1eb7t g\xf3c ngay tr\xean khe r\u1ed3i d\xf9ng R U2 R' (ho\u1eb7c F' U2 F) \u0111\u1ec3 bi\u1ebfn th\xe0nh tr\u01b0\u1eddng h\u1ee3p tr\u1eafng h\u01b0\u1edbng ngang, r\u1ed3i ch\xe8n nh\u01b0 th\u01b0\u1eddng."
e=l?'Both in the slot but wrong (flipped edge or twisted corner): that\'s the "Both in the slot" group in the F2L library \u2013 learning those 5 algorithms beats taking them out and re-pairing.':'C\u1ea3 hai n\u1eb1m trong khe nh\u01b0ng sai (c\u1ea1nh l\u1eadt ho\u1eb7c g\xf3c xoay): \u0111\xe2y l\xe0 nh\xf3m "C\u1ea3 hai trong khe" trong th\u01b0 vi\u1ec7n F2L \u2013 h\u1ecdc thu\u1ed9c 5 c\xf4ng th\u1ee9c n\xe0y c\xf2n nhanh h\u01a1n t\u1ef1 l\u1ea5y ra v\xe0 gh\xe9p l\u1ea1i.'
d=l?"Before pairing, turn U so the insert is just 3 moves (R U R' or F' U' F): one extra U is far cheaper than a long sequence.":"Tr\u01b0\u1edbc khi gh\xe9p, xoay U sao cho ch\xe8n \u0111\u01b0\u1ee3c b\u1eb1ng 3 b\u01b0\u1edbc (R U R' ho\u1eb7c F' U' F): m\u1ed9t l\u1ea7n U th\xeam r\u1ebb h\u01a1n nhi\u1ec1u so v\u1edbi m\u1ed9t chu\u1ed7i d\xe0i."
h=A.a([h,g,f,e,d,l?'Practice: use "Pick the easiest pair" to get used to scanning all 4 pairs, then the real-cube F2L drill for your slow cases.':'Luy\u1ec7n: d\xf9ng "Ch\u1ecdn c\u1eb7p d\u1ec5 nh\u1ea5t" \u0111\u1ec3 quen nh\xecn c\u1ea3 4 c\u1eb7p, r\u1ed3i "Luy\u1ec7n F2L tr\xean cube th\u1eadt" cho c\xe1c tr\u01b0\u1eddng h\u1ee3p c\xf2n ch\u1eadm.'],s)
l=$.c==="en"
g=l?"Pair stuck in front-left \u2192 front-right":"C\u1eb7p k\u1eb9t \u1edf khe tr\u01b0\u1edbc-tr\xe1i \u2192 khe tr\u01b0\u1edbc-ph\u1ea3i"
f=l?"White facing up":"G\xf3c tr\u1eafng h\u01b0\u1edbng l\xean"
l=l?"Both in slot, edge flipped":"C\u1ea3 hai trong khe, c\u1ea1nh l\u1eadt"
l=A.a([new A.b_("cfa10_stuck",g,"L' U L U' F' U' F",""),new A.b_("cfa10_up",f,"R U2 R' U' R U R'",""),new A.b_("cfa10_flip",l,"R U' R U2 F R2 F' U2 R2","")],k)
g=$.c==="en"
f=g?"Recognise OLL/PLL from two sides":"Nh\u1eadn di\u1ec7n OLL/PLL ch\u1ec9 v\u1edbi 2 m\u1eb7t"
e=g?"Know the case from the front and right sides \u2013 no U turns to peek.":"Nh\xecn m\u1eb7t tr\u01b0\u1edbc v\xe0 m\u1eb7t ph\u1ea3i l\xe0 bi\u1ebft tr\u01b0\u1eddng h\u1ee3p \u2013 kh\xf4ng c\u1ea7n xoay U \u0111\u1ec3 xem."
d=g?'PLL: look for "headlights" (2 same-colour corners on a side), a "bar" (3 same-colour stickers), a "checker" (alternating colours), a "block" (corner + edge of the same colour).':'PLL: t\xecm "\u0111\xe8n pha" (2 g\xf3c c\xf9ng m\xe0u \u1edf m\u1ed9t m\u1eb7t), "d\u1ea3i" (3 \xf4 c\xf9ng m\xe0u), "b\xe0n c\u1edd" (m\xe0u xen k\u1ebd), "kh\u1ed1i" (g\xf3c + c\u1ea1nh li\u1ec1n nhau c\xf9ng m\xe0u).'
c=g?"Two adjacent sides tell you every PLL \u2013 practise reading front + right, guess, then check.":"Hai m\u1eb7t k\u1ec1 nhau cho \u0111\u1ee7 th\xf4ng tin cho m\u1ecdi PLL \u2013 t\u1eadp nh\xecn tr\u01b0\u1edbc + ph\u1ea3i r\u1ed3i \u0111o\xe1n, sau \u0111\xf3 m\u1edbi xoay ki\u1ec3m tra."
b=g?"OLL: read the yellow shape on top first (dot, L, line, cross), then the yellow on the sides.":"OLL: nh\xecn h\xecnh v\xe0ng tr\xean m\u1eb7t tr\xean tr\u01b0\u1edbc (ch\u1ea5m, ch\u1eef L, \u0111\u01b0\u1eddng th\u1eb3ng, d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng), r\u1ed3i m\u1edbi xem m\xe0u v\xe0ng \u1edf m\u1eb7t b\xean."
d=A.a([d,c,b,g?"Practise: OLL/PLL recognition drill \u2013 build the longest correct streak you can.":"Luy\u1ec7n: Luy\u1ec7n nh\u1eadn di\u1ec7n OLL/PLL \u2013 tr\u1ea3 l\u1eddi \u0111\xfang li\xean ti\u1ebfp c\xe0ng nhi\u1ec1u c\xe0ng t\u1ed1t."],s)
g=$.c==="en"
c=g?"PLL + AUF: the U before and after":"PLL + AUF: xoay U tr\u01b0\u1edbc v\xe0 sau"
b=g?"Know straight away how to turn U before and after the PLL \u2013 no peeking turns.":"Bi\u1ebft ngay ph\u1ea3i xoay U th\u1ebf n\xe0o tr\u01b0\u1edbc v\xe0 sau PLL, kh\xf4ng ph\u1ea3i xoay th\u1eed."
a=g?"AUF (Adjust U Face) = turning the top to line it up. There are two: BEFORE the algorithm (put the case at its angle) and AFTER it (match the top layer to the rest).":"AUF (Adjust U Face) = xoay m\u1eb7t tr\xean cho kh\u1edbp. C\xf3 2 l\u1ea7n: TR\u01af\u1edaC c\xf4ng th\u1ee9c (\u0111\u1eb7t h\xecnh \u0111\xfang g\xf3c) v\xe0 SAU c\xf4ng th\u1ee9c (kh\u1edbp t\u1ea7ng tr\xean v\u1edbi 2 t\u1ea7ng d\u01b0\u1edbi)."
a0=g?"Before: use the headlights and bars to see how far the case is from its standard angle, then turn U exactly once.":"Tr\u01b0\u1edbc: nh\xecn \u0111\xe8n pha v\xe0 d\u1ea3i m\xe0u \u0111\u1ec3 bi\u1ebft h\xecnh \u0111ang l\u1ec7ch bao nhi\xeau so v\u1edbi h\xecnh chu\u1ea9n, r\u1ed3i xoay U \u0111\xfang m\u1ed9t l\u1ea7n."
a1=g?"Example T-perm: the headlights must be on the LEFT. Headlights at the back \u2192 U'; on the right \u2192 U2; at the front \u2192 U.":"V\xed d\u1ee5 T-perm: \u0111\xe8n pha ph\u1ea3i \u1edf b\xean TR\xc1I. \u0110\xe8n pha \u1edf sau \u2192 U'; \u1edf ph\u1ea3i \u2192 U2; \u1edf tr\u01b0\u1edbc \u2192 U."
a2=g?"After: when you recognise the PLL, note the front colour of the top layer \u2013 from it you can predict the final U before you finish.":"Sau: ngay l\xfac nh\u1eadn ra PLL, nh\u1edb m\xe0u m\u1eb7t tr\u01b0\u1edbc c\u1ee7a t\u1ea7ng tr\xean \u2013 t\u1eeb \u0111\xf3 \u0111o\xe1n \u0111\u01b0\u1ee3c U cu\u1ed1i tr\u01b0\u1edbc khi l\xe0m xong c\xf4ng th\u1ee9c."
a3=g?"H, Z, E, Na, Nb are symmetric: several angles work, pick the nearest.":"H, Z, E, Na, Nb \u0111\u1ed1i x\u1ee9ng: c\xf3 nhi\u1ec1u g\xf3c \u0111\xfang, ch\u1ecdn g\xf3c g\u1ea7n nh\u1ea5t."
a=A.a([a,a0,a1,a2,a3,g?'Practise: Recognition drill \u2192 PLL \u2192 turn on "Also ask the U turn".':'Luy\u1ec7n: Luy\u1ec7n nh\u1eadn d\u1ea1ng \u2192 PLL \u2192 b\u1eadt "H\u1ecfi c\u1ea3 xoay U".'],s)
k=A.a([new A.b_("tperm",$.c==="en"?"T-perm (headlights on the left)":"T-perm (\u0111\xe8n pha b\xean tr\xe1i)","R U R' U' R' F R2 U' R' U' R U R' F'",""),B.wl,B.Qr],k)
g=$.c==="en"
a0=g?"Cancel moves & predict the last U":"G\u1ed9p b\u01b0\u1edbc & \u0111o\xe1n tr\u01b0\u1edbc U cu\u1ed1i"
a1=g?"Remove wasted moves between algorithms and between OLL and PLL.":"B\u1ecf nh\u1eefng b\u01b0\u1edbc th\u1eeba gi\u1eefa hai c\xf4ng th\u1ee9c v\xe0 gi\u1eefa OLL v\u1edbi PLL."
a2=g?"If one algorithm ends on the same face the next begins, merge them: U then U \u2192 U2; R' then R \u2192 both cancel.":"C\xf4ng th\u1ee9c n\xe0y k\u1ebft th\xfac v\xe0 c\xf4ng th\u1ee9c sau b\u1eaft \u0111\u1ea7u b\u1eb1ng c\xf9ng m\u1ed9t m\u1eb7t th\xec g\u1ed9p: U r\u1ed3i U \u2192 U2; R' r\u1ed3i R \u2192 b\u1ecf c\u1ea3 hai."
a3=g?"During the last moves of OLL, watch the sides to recognise the PLL \u2013 no pause.":"Trong l\xfac l\xe0m v\xe0i b\u01b0\u1edbc cu\u1ed1i c\u1ee7a OLL, nh\xecn m\u1eb7t b\xean \u0111\u1ec3 nh\u1eadn ra PLL \u2013 kh\xf4ng d\u1eebng l\u1ea1i."
a4=g?"Predict the final U (AUF): once you know the PLL you also know how far off the top will be \u2013 do the last U without looking.":"\u0110o\xe1n tr\u01b0\u1edbc U cu\u1ed1i (AUF): khi nh\u1eadn ra PLL, \u0111\xe3 bi\u1ebft cube s\u1ebd l\u1ec7ch bao nhi\xeau sau \u0111\xf3 \u2013 l\xe0m U cu\u1ed1i ngay, kh\xf4ng c\u1ea7n nh\xecn l\u1ea1i."
a2=A.a([a2,a3,a4,g?"Keep your grip as long as possible: every regrip costs about 0.3 s.":"Gi\u1eef cube c\u1ed1 \u0111\u1ecbnh t\u1eeb \u0111\u1ea7u \u0111\u1ebfn cu\u1ed1i c\xe0ng l\xe2u c\xe0ng t\u1ed1t: m\u1ed7i l\u1ea7n \u0111\u1ed5i tay c\u1ea7m t\u1ed1n kho\u1ea3ng 0,3 gi\xe2y."],s)
g=$.c==="en"
a3=g?"Slow turning":"Gi\u1ea3i ch\u1eadm kh\xf4ng d\u1eebng (slow turning)"
a4=g?"Train look-ahead by turning slowly but steadily, never stopping.":"Luy\u1ec7n nh\xecn tr\u01b0\u1edbc b\u1eb1ng c\xe1ch xoay ch\u1eadm m\xe0 \u0111\u1ec1u, kh\xf4ng bao gi\u1edd d\u1eebng tay."
a5=g?"Why does slowing down make you faster? Most time is lost in the PAUSES while you search for pieces, not in hand speed.":"V\xec sao ch\u1eadm l\u1ea1i gi\xfap nhanh h\u01a1n? Ph\u1ea7n l\u1edbn th\u1eddi gian m\u1ea5t \u1edf nh\u1eefng l\xfac D\u1eeaNG \u0111\u1ec3 t\xecm m\u1ea3nh, kh\xf4ng ph\u1ea3i \u1edf t\u1ed1c \u0111\u1ed9 tay."
a6=g?"How: turn at 50\u201370% speed so you always see the next piece in advance. If you have to stop, you're still too fast \u2013 slow down more.":"C\xe1ch t\u1eadp: xoay \u1edf t\u1ed1c \u0111\u1ed9 50\u201370%, sao cho l\xfac n\xe0o c\u0169ng th\u1ea5y tr\u01b0\u1edbc m\u1ea3nh ti\u1ebfp theo. Ph\u1ea3i d\u1eebng = v\u1eabn qu\xe1 nhanh, gi\u1ea3m t\u1ed1c ti\u1ebfp."
a7=g?"Focus on F2L: while inserting one pair, your eyes find the next.":"T\u1eadp ph\u1ea7n F2L l\xe0 ch\xednh: trong l\xfac ch\xe8n c\u1eb7p n\xe0y, m\u1eaft t\xecm c\u1eb7p ti\u1ebfp theo."
a8=g?"Use a metronome: one move per beat, starting around 1\u20132 moves per second (the Look-ahead metronome screen).":"D\xf9ng m\xe1y \u0111\u1ebfm nh\u1ecbp: m\u1ed7i nh\u1ecbp m\u1ed9t b\u01b0\u1edbc, b\u1eaft \u0111\u1ea7u kho\u1ea3ng 1\u20132 b\u01b0\u1edbc/gi\xe2y (m\xe0n Nh\xecn tr\u01b0\u1edbc theo nh\u1ecbp)."
a5=A.a([a5,a6,a7,a8,g?"Do 5\u201310 slow solves a day before timing. After a few weeks your normal times usually drop.":"5\u201310 l\u01b0\u1ee3t ch\u1eadm m\u1ed7i ng\xe0y tr\u01b0\u1edbc khi b\u1ea5m gi\u1edd. Sau v\xe0i tu\u1ea7n, th\u1eddi gian b\xecnh th\u01b0\u1eddng th\u01b0\u1eddng gi\u1ea3m r\xf5."],s)
g=$.c==="en"
a6=g?"Last slot: insert so the yellow cross is already made":"Khe cu\u1ed1i: ch\xe8n sao cho ra s\u1eb5n d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng v\xe0ng"
a7=g?"Choose how to insert the last pair so OLL gets easier \u2013 your first step into edge control.":"Ch\u1ecdn c\xe1ch ch\xe8n c\u1eb7p cu\u1ed1i \u0111\u1ec3 OLL d\u1ec5 h\u01a1n \u2013 b\u01b0\u1edbc \u0111\u1ea7u c\u1ee7a edge control."
a8=g?"With one slot left, look at the top before inserting: count the yellow edges facing up.":"Khi ch\u1ec9 c\xf2n m\u1ed9t khe, nh\xecn t\u1ea7ng tr\xean tr\u01b0\u1edbc khi ch\xe8n: \u0111\u1ebfm c\u1ea1nh v\xe0ng \u0111ang h\u01b0\u1edbng l\xean."
a9=g?"Inserting with only R and U never flips an edge. Inserts with F or F' (e.g. F' U' F, R' F R F') do flip edges \u2013 that's how you change the number of yellow edges up.":"Ch\xe8n ch\u1ec9 b\u1eb1ng R v\xe0 U kh\xf4ng l\u1eadt c\u1ea1nh n\xe0o. Ch\xe8n c\xf3 F ho\u1eb7c F' (vd F' U' F, R' F R F') th\xec l\u1eadt c\u1ea1nh \u2013 \u0111\xf3 l\xe0 c\xe1ch \u0111\u1ed5i s\u1ed1 c\u1ea1nh v\xe0ng h\u01b0\u1edbng l\xean."
b0=g?"One pair can usually be inserted a few ways. Pick the one that leaves all 4 yellow edges: OLL is then corners only (7 familiar cases like Sune) \u2013 no yellow-cross step from 2-look.":"C\xf9ng m\u1ed9t c\u1eb7p th\u01b0\u1eddng ch\xe8n \u0111\u01b0\u1ee3c v\xe0i c\xe1ch. Ch\u1ecdn c\xe1ch \u0111\u1ec3 l\u1ea1i \u0111\u1ee7 4 c\u1ea1nh v\xe0ng: OLL ch\u1ec9 c\xf2n xoay g\xf3c (7 tr\u01b0\u1eddng h\u1ee3p quen thu\u1ed9c nh\u01b0 Sune), b\u1ecf h\u1eb3n b\u01b0\u1edbc d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng v\xe0ng c\u1ee7a 2-look."
a8=A.a([a8,a9,b0,g?'No memorising needed: train with the "Last slot" drill until your eyes compare options naturally. Best once you know 2-look and solve around sub-30.':'Kh\xf4ng c\u1ea7n h\u1ecdc thu\u1ed9c: luy\u1ec7n b\u1eb1ng b\xe0i "Khe cu\u1ed1i" \u0111\u1ec3 m\u1eaft quen so s\xe1nh. D\xe0nh cho khi \u0111\xe3 thu\u1ed9c 2-look v\xe0 gi\u1ea3i d\u01b0\u1edbi kho\u1ea3ng 30 gi\xe2y.'],s)
g=$.c==="en"
a9=g?"The road to sub-20":"L\u1ed9 tr\xecnh xu\u1ed1ng d\u01b0\u1edbi 20 gi\xe2y"
b0=g?"Know what to learn after 2-look, in the most useful order.":"Bi\u1ebft h\u1ecdc g\xec ti\u1ebfp theo sau 2-look, theo th\u1ee9 t\u1ef1 hi\u1ec7u qu\u1ea3 nh\u1ea5t."
b1=g?"1. All 21 PLLs first: they help on EVERY solve. Then the 57 OLLs.":"1. \u0110\u1ee7 21 PLL tr\u01b0\u1edbc: d\xf9ng \u0111\u01b0\u1ee3c \u1edf M\u1eccI l\u01b0\u1ee3t gi\u1ea3i. Sau \u0111\xf3 57 OLL."
